# Copy to .env.local for development, or set these in your host's dashboard.
# Everything except GEMINI_API_KEY is optional: the feature it powers says
# plainly that it is not set up rather than pretending to work.

# --- Required: the AI itself -------------------------------------------------
# From https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to a current Flash model; only set this to pin a version.
# GEMINI_MODEL=

# --- Sign-in (Supabase) ------------------------------------------------------
# The main way in, and the one that works on a filtered school network: the
# browser only ever talks to your own Supabase subdomain, never to
# accounts.google.com.
#   1. Make a project at https://supabase.com
#   2. Settings -> API Keys -> copy the "Project URL" and the "Publishable key"
#      (older projects call the same thing the "anon public" key). Do NOT use
#      the direct connection string: that holds the database password.
#   3. Authentication -> Providers -> Email is on by default. Turning OFF
#      "Confirm email" lets students sign in immediately instead of waiting
#      for a link, which is usually what you want for a class.
#   4. Optional: Authentication -> Providers -> Google, to offer that too.
#      Set the redirect to https://your-site/ and note that this still sends
#      students to accounts.google.com, so it stays blocked where that is.
# Neither value is a secret: the anon key is what every browser using the
# project sends, and row-level security is what guards the data behind it.
SUPABASE_URL=
# Either name works; they hold the same value.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --- Google sign-in (fallback) -----------------------------------------------
# Only used when Supabase is not configured above. Loads a script from
# accounts.google.com, which school filters routinely block.
# Google Cloud Console -> Credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Web application.
# Add your site to "Authorized JavaScript origins" (NOT redirect URIs).
# The browser fetches this from /api/auth/config at runtime, so there is no
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ copy to keep in sync.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# --- Search tab --------------------------------------------------------------
# Google refuses to be framed, so search runs through Programmable Search and
# renders results in the app.
#   1. Make an engine at https://programmablesearchengine.google.com (whole web)
#   2. Enable "Custom Search API" on the project the key belongs to
GOOGLE_CSE_ID=
GOOGLE_CSE_KEY=

# --- Watch tab ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Needs "YouTube Data API v3" enabled on the project. An AI Studio key will NOT
# work here: it is scoped to the Generative Language API only.
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# --- Canvas LMS --------------------------------------------------------------
# A developer key from whoever administers your school's Canvas. Students never
# see a token or a password; this is real OAuth2.
# The redirect URI must exactly match the one on the developer key, and must
# point at https://your-site/api/canvas/callback
CANVAS_CLIENT_ID=
CANVAS_CLIENT_SECRET=
CANVAS_REDIRECT_URI=
